REST = REpresentational State Transfer. Scary name, simple idea:

It's just a style/set of rules for building APIs (ways for apps to talk to each other over the internet).
Everything is treated as a "resource" — like a user, a blog post, a product. Each resource has its own URL address.
You use HTTP methods (like verbs) to say what you want to do to that resource.
RESTFUL APIs : A RESTful API (Representational State Transfer) is an architectural style that allows different computer systems to exchange data securely and predictably over the internet. It acts as a standardized translator, enabling applications like a mobile app, a website, and a backend server to talk to each other using the existing rules of HTTP
